From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] misc: add an experiment-only Gemini lid EINT delivery
 probe

The Gemini lid on GPIO66 changes level while gpio-keys, which requests a
both-edge interrupt emulated by polarity flipping, never sees EINT5. The
vendor kernel uses a level-triggered interrupt on the same pin.

Behind a default-off option, own the lid GPIO and its interrupt through
the standard GPIO and IRQ APIs and request one level-low interrupt, left
disabled. A write-once debugfs "arm" file opens one finite window, only
while the line reads high. The first delivery is masked in hard-IRQ
context and never re-enabled; a timeout disarms the window otherwise. A
read-only "status" file reports the outcome, levels and timing. There is
no polarity alternation, software trigger, wake or suspend handling.

Unsigned experiment draft; archive identity is non-certifying.
---
 drivers/misc/Kconfig                 |  12 ++
 drivers/misc/Makefile                |   1 +
 drivers/misc/gemini-lid-eint-probe.c | 238 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 251 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/gemini-lid-eint-probe.c

diff --git a/drivers/misc/Kconfig b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
index 00683bf06..939c09919 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
@@ -644,6 +644,18 @@ config MCHP_LAN966X_PCI
 	    - lan966x-miim (MDIO_MSCC_MIIM)
 	    - lan966x-switch (LAN966X_SWITCH)
 
+config GEMINI_LID_EINT_PROBE
+	bool "Gemini lid one-shot EINT delivery probe (experiment)"
+	depends on OF && GPIOLIB && DEBUG_FS
+	help
+	  Experiment-only diagnostic for the Gemini PDA lid sensor. Owns the
+	  lid GPIO and its EINT, and lets root arm one finite window in which
+	  the first level-low interrupt is recorded and immediately masked.
+	  It never re-enables the line, alternates polarity or triggers an
+	  interrupt in software.
+
+	  If unsure, say N.
+
 source "drivers/misc/c2port/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/eeprom/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/cb710/Kconfig"
